# Shell scripts run under Git Bash and WSL; CRLF breaks the shebang and every
# quoted string. Enforce LF regardless of the editor or tool that wrote them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Vendored dependencies are exempt from that rule, and this is not cosmetic.
# The OpenZeppelin scripts under contracts/lib were committed with CRLF before
# the rule above existed. Git then normalises them to LF on checkout and diffs
# that against the CRLF blobs in HEAD, so all 17 report as modified forever:
# no checkout, stash, reset or core.fileMode change settles it, and every pull
# aborts with "local changes would be overwritten". They are OpenZeppelin's own
# release tooling and nothing in this repository runs them, so the shebang
# argument above does not apply. Leave their bytes alone.
sidequest-protocol/contracts/lib/** -text
